<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>“Lord, Thou hast here Thy ninety and nine;</l><l>Are they not enough for Thee?”</l><l>But the Shepherd made answer: “This of Mine</l><l>Has wandered away from Me;</l><l>And although the road be rough and steep,</l><l>I go to the desert to find My sheep.”</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>But none of the ransomed ever knew</l><l>How deep were the waters crossed;</l><l>Nor how dark was the night which the Lord passed through</l><l>Ere He found His sheep that was lost.</l><l>Out in the bleak desert He heard its cry—</l><l>All bleeding and helpless, and ready to die.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>“Lord, whence are those blood-drops all the way</l><l>That mark out the mountain’s track?”</l><l>“They were shed for one who had gone astray</l><l>Ere the Shepherd could bring him back.”</l><l>“Lord, whence are Thy hands so rent and torn?”</l><l>“They’re pierced tonight by many a thorn.”</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
